  "instruction": "Using Visual Studio Code, create a Python script named `amazon_rf_classification.py` in the `/home/user/analysis_results/` directory. The dataset `amazon_commerce_reviews.csv` is already located in the same directory. In this script, load the dataset using pandas. Train a Random Forest classifier using V1–V1000 as predictors and Class as the target. Use 5-fold cross-validation to evaluate the model. Report the mean accuracy, macro-F1 score, and top-5 accuracy across folds. Save the results to a text file named `rf_classification_results.txt`, containing one line per metric in the format: Accuracy: <value>, Macro_F1: <value>, Top5_Accuracy: <value>. Round all metric values to four decimal places.",
